.vs
.vscode
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
bin
obj
.idea
*.binlog
build_errors.txt
run_errors.txt
*.exe
*.dll

.opencode/
.claude/
vscode-extension/bun.lock
# BenchmarkDotNet writes to <cwd>/BenchmarkDotNet.Artifacts, and the documented way to run the
# suite is from src/, so artifacts land in src/ — not next to the benchmark project. The old
# pattern pointed at a directory that is never created, which is how stale results for benchmarks
# that no longer exist ended up committed.
**/BenchmarkDotNet.Artifacts/
# Transpiler output. `--emit-c` writes .prolang/artifacts/ and `--emit-psp` writes .prolang/psp/,
# both containing generated C, copies of the native/ runtime headers, and build scripts — all
# reproducible from the .prl source. The rule previously named artifacts/ only, so the PSP output
# was committed and then churned on every --emit-psp run.
**/.prolang/
*.obj
*.runtimeconfig.json
*.deps.json
build/

# Compiled output from running the compiler over examples/ and tests/. The .prl files are the
# sources; the assemblies beside them are throwaway. Several of these were committed before the
# *.dll and *.runtimeconfig.json rules existed, so they stayed tracked — a .gitignore entry has
# no effect on a file git is already following.
examples/**/bin/
tests/**/output_folder/
*.decompiled.cs

# Scratch directories created by ProLang.Tests. Tests write build output under the system temp
# folder, never into the source tree, but pin this in case TMP is ever pointed at the repo.
prolang-tests/

# Generated baselines for ProLang.Tests: disassembled IL listings and captured program stdout.
# Regenerate with:  PROLANG_UPDATE_SNAPSHOTS=1 dotnet test src/ProLang.Tests/ProLang.Tests.csproj
# Note these are the comparison targets for IlSnapshotTests and ExecutionTests, so on a fresh
# clone both report "No snapshot at ..." until they have been regenerated locally.
src/ProLang.Tests/Snapshots/
src/ProLang.Tests/Expected/
**/CMakeFiles
*.a
native/CMakeCache.txt
native/Makefile
native/cmake_install.cmake
